      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nEFI Main Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 6 / A28 - low-side (Aux 5-8 capable of either; low-side chosen for ECU Hold Power)\nEFI Main Relay 86: Coil + - PERMANENT battery via F12 5A (must stay live after key-off for Hold Power)\nETB Power Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 2 / A20 - LOW-SIDE ONLY (Aux 1-4)\nETB Power Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nFuel Pump Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 3 / A19 - LOW-SIDE ONLY (Aux 1-4)\nFuel Pump Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nRadiator Fan Relay (on/off) 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nStart Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nBulkhead A - firewall (HDP24-2 1: spare (size 16) - was the shared shield drain, retired by 6.32\nBulkhead A - firewall (HDP24-2 35: MRS EPS pump logic enable - cabin fuse block c14 (7.5A, ignition-switched); moved from bulkhead B c14 2026-09-28 (the pump's ECU signal is A27)\nsp_5v (Splice): +5V at ECU A (A32 lead 18 AWG) - feeds sp_5v_bha before bulkhead A (c2, c39, c40 at 20 AWG), an 18 AWG trunk to sp_5v_b on ST185-B-cabin (broken off), crossover (a), and an 18 AWG link to sp_5v_2\nsp_5v_2 (Splice): +5V cabin loads off sp_5v - APS, cruise ladder, w210 (20 AWG each)\nsp_gndout (Splice): Gnd Out at ECU A (A24 lead 18 AWG) - feeds sp_gnd_bha before bulkhead A (c3, c41-c44 at 20 AWG) for the A loads only; loom B's sensors return to their own Gnd Out, ECU B22 (no A24-B22 tie in the harness)\nsp_sw12 (Splice): switched 12V bus - its B-side loads (condenser fan and EPS relay coils, VSS feed on bulkhead B c20) are drawn on ST185-B-cabin (broken off)\nsp_chassis (Splice): cabin chassis ground - ECU-B B25/B34 join it on ST185-B-cabin (broken off)",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 4200,
        "y": 0
      }
    }
  ],
